      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "arc.plant.05a",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "No deal that splits the 340. The assembly decides, not the minister, not a union, and we spread the fight to other plants."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "arc.plant.06",
        "option": "everyone"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "arc.plant.07",
        "option": "capital"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "challenge:tension.one-workforce-no-union",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "The workers doing it themselves, in the wildcats and the circle. No union or party does it for us. That's the whole point."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "module.trajectory.from",
        "option": "radical"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.01",
        "affordance": "reject",
        "premise": "not-mine",
        "text": "I would never be a minister. Ministers manage capital for a national economy; workers and peasants there have to take it into their own hands."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.02",
        "option": "cold-war"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.03",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "Neither British nor Iranian oil capital. Oil workers running things themselves; a nationalist premier just swaps the boss for the state."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.04",
        "option": "class"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.05",
        "option": "workers"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.06",
        "option": "ordinary"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.07",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "Not my call and not my choice between creditors. Every one is national capital shopping for a patron. The railway workers decide whether it gets built and for whom."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.08",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "The list is a menu for national capital. Cutting loose just closes the nation around its own bosses; I'd say none of it solves the wage relation."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.09",
        "option": "victims"
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.10",
        "affordance": "none",
        "text": "It's a word for capital accumulation. Real answer: abolishing wage labour, which means workers running production themselves."
      },
      {
        "t": "answer",
        "node": "descent.development.11",
        "option": "capital"
      },
